{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1525201191,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMTkyOTE1OTA=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2466","origin":"github"},"title":"Incorrect/confusing comment in .datalad/.gitattributes","message":"The comment in .datalad/.gitattributes looks wrong.\n\n```bash\n% datalad create foods\n% cat foods/.datalad/.gitattributes\n# Text files (according to file --mime-type) are added directly to git.\n# See http://git-annex.branchable.com/tips/largefiles/ for more info.\n** annex.largefiles=nothing\nmetadata/objects/** annex.largefiles=(largerthan=20kb)\n```\n\nIf I'm reading these attributes correctly, they say to add files (not just text files) directly to git if they are anywhere within the .datalad subdirectory except metadata/objects.  If the file is in .datalad/metadata/objects, add it directly to git unless it is larger than 20kb.\n\nI think the comment should be moved above the content that `create --text-no-annex` writes:\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/b5c67a4b5e0d02c5ad1bffdfffe5f4a21e0462b7/datalad/distribution/create.py#L342-L344\n\nOr just deleted altogether.","files":null}]}